     This is misleading, or perhaps just sloppy use of terminology.
If a gem is identified you'll know its curse/bless state and other
similar properties (if there are any that are applicable to gems)
like rustproofing.  For shop transactions, you only need the gem
type to be discovered, not the individual gem be identified.  So
"a diamond" will be eligible for full value; "a white gem" and "a
white gem called I'm sure this is a diamond" will not.  You don't
need the inventory display showing "an uncursed diamond".

     Once you've discovered the type, other objects of that same
type will be recognized (relevant here since your list of ways to
ID doesn't mention this) unless the new one hasn't been seen yet
because it was picked up while you're blind.


